1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
Seriously? Cutting in without a signal?

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,833
That's illegal! Illegal!

3
00:00:02,833 --> 00:00:04,600
Dad, you didn't signal just now either.

4
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,067
I'm fine. So what~

5
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:10,733
When I do it, so what. When you do it, illegal. Double standard, number one.

6
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:12,433
I'm… Modapman.

7
00:00:14,233 --> 00:00:18,200
Case summary. Saturday morning. Destination: the supermarket.

8
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,967
Drive nicely today.

9
00:00:19,967 --> 00:00:22,333
Who follows the law better than me?

10
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:23,633
Plenty of people.

11
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:26,800
Just three rounds. Round one: cutting in.

12
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:28,700
Look! He just slid in at the very front!

13
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,133
Apologize to everyone in line! Apologize!

14
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:31,700
Five minutes later.

15
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,200
…Honey, where are you going?

16
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,567
This isn't cutting. I just eased in a little.

17
00:00:35,567 --> 00:00:37,067
Double standard, number two.

18
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:39,633
Sir, a little is still cutting in.

19
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:41,567
You can't squeeze in between cars waiting in line.

20
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:44,200
That's a 30,000 won fine and 10 penalty points.

21
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:44,700
…Huh?

22
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:48,333
Round two: turn signals. Right in the middle of a crackdown.

23
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:50,600
Moragu, a turn signal is a conversation.

24
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,300
It says, 'I'm coming in~'

25
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,733
Then what did you say back there?

26
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:57,233
I… signaled in my heart.

27
00:00:57,233 --> 00:00:58,933
Double standard, number three.

28
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:01,133
Your heart doesn't show up on camera.

29
00:01:01,133 --> 00:01:03,900
Turn it on 30 meters before you change lanes.

30
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:07,167
Honey, even the model answer can't save you here.

31
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:11,300
Round three: parking. Location: in front of the supermarket.

32
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:13,467
Parked in front of a fire hydrant? Report him right now!

33
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:14,900
Why can't you park there?

34
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,767
Because that's where fire trucks get water when there's a fire.

35
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:20,367
Three minutes later. The parking lot is full.

36
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:22,367
Just one minute. So what~

37
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:24,100
Double standard, number four.

38
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:24,967
…We meet again.

39
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:26,700
I do grocery shopping too.

40
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,800
No parking within 5 meters of a fire hydrant.

41
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:31,400
A report takes two photos, one minute apart.

42
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,667
So one minute is plenty. For the report.

43
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:35,133
…Huh?

44
00:01:35,933 --> 00:01:40,133
Dad, the line, the signal, the hydrant…

45
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,233
They're all for other people.

46
00:01:42,233 --> 00:01:46,333
…You're right. In a fire, every second counts.

47
00:01:46,333 --> 00:01:49,900
Then don't say 'so what.' Say 'what about them?'

48
00:01:49,967 --> 00:01:52,400
Think first about how others will feel?

49
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,467
Yeah. That's what a conversation is.

50
00:01:54,733 --> 00:01:55,400
On the way home.

51
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,300
Okay, from now on I always signal!

52
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:58,567
Two kilometers later.

53
00:01:58,567 --> 00:02:00,933
Honey, your signal is still on.

54
00:02:00,933 --> 00:02:03,400
Dad, this time you left it on too long.

55
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:06,233
That's not a double standard. Just a wrong answer.

56
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:08,633
…Modapman, as always.
